# TODO - CUDA exact VM adapter

## Objective

Implement the first GPU adapter with exact discrete Malbolge semantics and
massively parallel independent VM execution for candidate evaluation and test
batches.

## Acceptance

- CUDA kernels implement exact discrete VM semantics for independent batches and
  are differentially checked against the CPU reference across randomized and
  boundary-heavy corpora.
- A CPU/reference path remains sufficient for correctness, and accelerator
  failure/unavailability changes performance rather than semantic acceptance.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `accelerator/`, `algorithms/`,
  `optimizer/`, `benchmarks/accelerator/`, `tests/optimizer/`.
- Required evidence: CPU/reference differential results, device/resource
  metadata, failure/fallback tests, and benchmark samples for claimed speedups.
- Active foundation: integer-only CUDA kernels implement exact classic
  rotate/crazy batches through NVRTC + Driver API behind the shared accelerator
  port. CUDA 13.3 Update 1 redistributables are reproducibly pinned by component
  path/version/SHA-256; the active Python adapter uses standard-library `ctypes`
  only.
- Compact classic one-step VM execution is now active. A fixed-width request
  declares registers/counters/input plus at most four keyed memory cells; CUDA
  returns the full `StepTrace`-equivalent projection. Rust integration compares
  fourteen instruction/edge fixtures directly with normative
  `Machine::step_traced()`, including atomic rejection and write aliasing.
- Resident classic bounded execution is active behind
  `ClassicRunRequest`/`ClassicRunResult`: one CUDA thread keeps one complete
  59,049-word state resident for its full budget. `tests/vm/cuda_run.rs` compares
  nine results against normative Rust across every final memory word plus
  registers, I/O, termination, steps, resumption, wrap, aliasing, and atomic
  rejection. RTX 4060 (`sm_89`) development evidence passes this differential.
- Current-profile resident coverage is now active behind explicit scalable
  geometry. `tests/vm/cuda_profile_run.rs` supplies canonical geometry from Rust
  and compares eight complete `malbolge-2026.2` results across all 4,782,969 final
  words plus registers, I/O, termination, steps, wrap, and atomic rejection on the
  RTX 4060 (`sm_89`).
- Product-level batch routing is active. The retained RTX 4060 baseline reached
  about 40.08 VMs/s at current-profile batch 32; device-side shared initialization
  now reaches about 51.67 VMs/s and cuts median upload time about 6.93x. Persistent
  scalable sessions reach about 2.00 million 64-step VM segments/s at batch 128
  when setup/observation/snapshots are outside the timed region. Reusable validated
  profile memory then raises retained complete-snapshot batch 32 to about
  93.68 VMs/s while validation/planning falls to about 0.23 ms. Direct snapshot
  output removes redundant packed host staging. Exact classic crazy/rotate
  candidate evaluation now traverses the hardware-neutral work port on live CUDA
  and matches CPU evidence over 257-item deterministic corpora. Exact candidate
  evidence can now feed verification-assist hints through live CUDA over a
  deterministic 257-item rotate corpus while trusted admission remains separate;
  malformed optional evidence becomes no hint. The bounded
  `classic-rotate-target-search-v1` strategy now evaluates a deterministic
  257-candidate corpus through live CUDA, records CUDA as actual search execution,
  matches the CPU reference proposals, and leaves final admission to the CPU
  verifier. The retained complete-domain benchmark covers 59,049 candidates with
  15 samples per backend. CPU median is 401.185 ms and CUDA median is 412.570 ms
  on the RTX 4060, yielding 0.972x CUDA/CPU and rejecting the speedup hypothesis
  for this host-heavy route while every proposal remains exact. Broader live
  hardware, resident search, and synthesis/search strategies remain open.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `replaceable-accelerator-boundary`,
  `batch-vm-execution`.
